/tmp/tmp.Ioo7zIpwO3/src/Revision_main.tex:497:\begin{theorem}\label{thm:GBasis} 
/tmp/tmp.Ioo7zIpwO3/src/Revision_main.tex:499:Then, the reduced Gröbner basis of the ideal $I_{n,k} = (x_1^2, \dots, x_n^2, (x_1 + \cdots + x_n)^k)$ with respect to any term ordering that, after any permutation of the first $k$ variables and a suitable set of transpositions of the form $(k+2i - 1,k+ 2i)$ for $i\geq 1$, satisfies $x_1 \succ \cdots \succ x_n$, is given by
